AIM:- Given the head of a singly linked list, return true if it is a palindrome or false otherwise.
ALGORITHM :-
The easiest method is to use two pointers and reverse the second half of the linked list.

Set two pointers:
slow = head
fast = head
Move slow one step and fast two steps at a time.
When fast reaches the end, slow will be at the middle of the list.
Reverse the linked list starting from slow.
Set:
left = head
right = reversed second half
Compare the values of left and right one by one.
If any values are different, return false.
If all corresponding values are the same, return true.

CODE:-
class Solution {
public:
    bool isPalindrome(ListNode* head) {
        vector<int> arr;

        // Store values in array
        while (head != NULL) {
            arr.push_back(head->val);
            head = head->next;
        }

        // Check palindrome
        int i = 0;
        int j = arr.size() - 1;

        while (i < j) {
            if (arr[i] != arr[j])
                return false;

            i++;
            j--;
        }

        return true;
    }
};
